@prefix lgo:  <https://legalgraph.org/ontology#> .
@prefix lgv:  <https://legalgraph.org/vocab/> .
@prefix lg:  <https://legalgraph.org/id/> .
@prefix eli:  <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Portugal: Article 10 of Decree-Law 7/2004 (additions to data/extracted/pt/).

lg:PT-DL-7-2004
    eli:title "Decree-Law No. 7/2004 on electronic commerce"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "DL 7/2004" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2000-31 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.pgdlisboa.pt/leis/lei_mostra_articulado.php?nid=1399&tabela=leis> ;
    rdfs:comment "Portugal requires the fiscal identification number (NIF) of every provider — item d) has no 'where applicable' — and puts the authorisation, profession and costs duties in their own numbered paragraphs. The source is the consolidated text published by the Lisbon District Prosecutor's Office (PGDL); dre.pt is a JavaScript application."@en .
lg:PT-CSC
    eli:title "Código das Sociedades Comerciais"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "CSC" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2017-1132 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.pgdlisboa.pt/leis/lei_mostra_articulado.php?nid=524&tabela=leis> ;
    rdfs:comment "Artigo 171 requires companies to state on websites and all external activity: firm name, type, seat, registry office, registration number, corporate identification number and liquidation status; n.º 2 adds capital disclosures for quota, public and share-commandite companies; n.º 3 covers foreign branches."@en .

lg:PT-LEI-144-2015
    lgo:shortName "Lei 144/2015" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2013-11 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.pgdlisboa.pt/leis/lei_mostra_articulado.php?nid=2425&tabela=leis> ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 18 transposes art. 13 of the ADR Directive: suppliers established in Portugal bound to an ADR entity (by adhesion or mandatory arbitration) must name it and give its website on their own site where they have one, and in written or adhesion contracts or another durable medium."@en .
